<LegalPage title="Privacy notice" description="What MyAvedan collects, why, and how to delete it." updated="17 November 2026">
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can browse and search MyAvedan without an account.</li>
    <li>The eligibility checker runs in your browser. Your date of birth, category and qualification are not sent to us or stored.</li>
    <li>We never ask for Aadhaar numbers, passwords, OTPs, bank details or logins for government portals.</li>
    <li>We never send your personal details to an AI service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p><strong>When you browse:</strong> basic, cookie-free usage statistics (pages viewed, approximate region, device type) to see which features help people. These do not identify you.</p>
  <p><strong>When you report an error:</strong> the notice, the part you flagged and your message. We ask you not to include personal details.</p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you create an account (coming later):</strong> your email address from Google sign-in, the opportunities you save, your
    reminder choices and any preferences you choose to give. Date of birth and category are stored only if you switch on eligibility
    matching, and we explain why before asking.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Server logs: up to 30 days.</li>
    <li>Error reports: until the report is resolved, then kept without any personal content as part of the change history.</li>
    <li>Account data: until you delete your account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Turn reminders off at any time.</li>
    <li>Delete your account and all saved data from your dashboard. Deletion is permanent.</li>
    <li>Ask us what we hold about you using the contact details on the <a href="/about/#contact">About page</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who runs MyAvedan</h2>
  <p>MyAvedan is operated by TrutiAI. Contact: <a href="mailto:akhill6174dwivedi@gmail.com">akhill6174dwivedi@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
